  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MoU with IOM for multiple typhoons in Philippines 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Typhoon Tino caused significant impact across the Philippines. Between 2-5 November, the typhoon made multiple landfalls across the central Philippines (Visayas) with wind speeds equivalent to a Category 2 hurricane. An estimated 4.2 million people have been affected compounding the impacts of multiple recent typhoons, floods, and two earthquakes in the same region. Flash floods contributed to the high death toll, with over 230 dead and over 100 people still missing. Over 350,000 people are displaced. For some, such as in Cebu and Negros Occidental, this is expected to be protracted given widespread flooding destroyed 25,000 houses and damaged 200,000 houses and infrastructure. Through IOM, FCDO will be providing shelter, NFIs and WASH to the worst affected areas.</narrative>
  </description>
